{# ============================================================================
   SETTINGS — the six answers this module cannot guess about an organisation,
   ported from the design's configure.html#settings, plus the shift vocabulary
   and the check-in statuses list.

   EVERY ONE OF THESE WAS AN OPEN VERDICT while the module was being designed.
   They are fields now, each with its default and the CONSEQUENCE of choosing
   wrong stated beside it — which is the only honest way to ship a question
   nobody could answer on somebody else's behalf. The consequence text is not
   decoration and it is not an essay: it is the one fact that makes the field
   answerable.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/configure/_frame.html.twig' %}

{% block roster_section %}
<form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SAVE_SETTINGS_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <div class="c rband">
        {# HEADER = IDENTITY ONLY, no door: ruled 2026-09-20. #}
        <div class="rb-hd">
            <span class="tab">Settings</span>
            <span class="rb-ttl">the answers this module cannot guess &mdash; each with the consequence of getting it wrong</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rb-body">

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Ping interval</b><em>positions per hour, per handset</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="ping_interval_minutes" value="{{ settings.pingIntervalMinutes }}" aria-label="Ping interval in minutes" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                    <span class="unit">minutes</span>
                    <span class="unit">default {{ constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\DependencyInjection\\RosterConfiguration::DEFAULT_PING_INTERVAL_MINUTES') }}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>It trades against the catchment.</b> A wide catchment tolerates a slow interval; a tight one does not &mdash; at 2 km and 60 min a ranger can leave and return unseen. Every minute you take off it costs battery in a place with no mains.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Off days on a tour</b><em>what an off day in a cycle produces</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    <span class="rsw">
                        <label class="{{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? 'on' : '' }}"><input type="radio" name="off_day_has_no_state" value="1" {{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? 'checked' : '' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>no state</label>
                        <label class="{{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? '' : 'on' }}"><input type="radio" name="off_day_has_no_state" value="0" {{ settings.offDayHasNoState ? '' : 'checked' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>no check-in</label>
                    </span>
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>Default: no state.</b> A ranger the ring stands down is not expected to check in and has failed at nothing. Choose <i>no check-in</i> only if this organisation requires a daily check-in from everyone, on or off &mdash; it will colour every rest day red.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Leave approval</b><em>a request, an approver, a state machine</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    <span class="rsw">
                        <label class="{{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? '' : 'on' }}"><input type="radio" name="leave_approval_shown" value="0" {{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? '' : 'checked' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>off</label>
                        <label class="{{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? 'on' : '' }}"><input type="radio" name="leave_approval_shown" value="1" {{ settings.leaveApprovalShown ? 'checked' : '' }} {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>on</label>
                    </span>
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>Default: off.</b> The roster records an ABSENCE &mdash; person, from, to, kind, recorded by &mdash; because the hole it makes is this module&rsquo;s to show. Approval belongs to Team; turning it on here adds only a read-only state chip on the absence row.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Shift vocabulary</b><em>the named shifts and their windows</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    {% for shift in shifts %}
                        <span class="r-sh {{ shift.isOpen ? '' : 'closed' }}"><i></i>{{ shift.label|lower }} {{ shift.startsAt }}&ndash;{{ shift.endsAt }}</span>
                    {% endfor %}
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>One list for the whole area.</b> Every rotation, every rota cell and every day-board block reads from it, so a fifth shift is a fifth chip everywhere and nothing has to be redrawn. A shift in use cannot be deleted, only closed.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Default catchment</b><em>used by a post that sets none of its own</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="default_catchment_metres" value="{{ settings.defaultCatchmentMetres }}" aria-label="Default catchment in metres" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                    <span class="unit">m</span>
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>It decides who reads as unverified.</b> A radius smaller than the post&rsquo;s own compound will flag people who are standing in it; one larger than the nearest road will verify people driving past. Changing it <b>re-derives every past day</b>, because a state is never stored. It is the ring a post falls back on: verification measures against the POST&rsquo;s own catchment, and a post that sets none takes this.</span>
            </div>

            <div class="rset">
                <span class="lb"><b>Late and vacancy thresholds</b><em>when a post reads late, and when a hole is announced</em></span>
                <span class="ct">
                    <select class="fld" name="late_threshold" aria-label="Late threshold" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        {% for threshold in lateThresholds %}
                            <option value="{{ threshold.value }}" {{ threshold == settings.lateThreshold ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ threshold.label }}</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                    <select class="fld" name="vacancy_announce" aria-label="When a hole is announced" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        {% for announce in vacancyAnnouncements %}
                            <option value="{{ announce.value }}" {{ announce == settings.vacancyAnnounce ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ announce.label }}</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                </span>
                <span class="why"><b>Late is per post</b> and falls back to twice its ping interval; a post may override it on the Watches section. <b>A hole is announced as soon as it is known</b> &mdash; an unfit check-in at 05:58 makes tonight&rsquo;s hole visible at 05:58, not at 18:00.</span>
            </div>


            {# Save at the END of the form body, right-aligned — the house's
               own .staddrow, not a footer strip. #}
            {% if mayManage %}
                <div class="staddrow"><span class="sp"></span><button type="submit" class="cta">Save settings</button></div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
</form>

{# THE CHECK-IN STATUSES A RANGER IS OFFERED are the AREA's list, not this
   module's: the check-in belongs to the area, and so do the statuses it can
   carry. The design puts them on this page because this is where somebody
   configuring the roster looks for them — read here, written there.

   READ, ORDERED, RETIRED ROWS DIMMED AND KEPT. Each one carries the KIND the
   platform reasons about, which is what says why "at post" is the only
   status a verified/unverified reading can come from. #}
<div style="height:12px"></div>
<div class="c rband">
    <div class="rb-hd">
        <span class="tab">Check-in statuses</span>
        <span class="rb-ttl">what a ranger is offered on the handset &mdash; the <b>area&rsquo;s</b> list, read here and written there</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rb-body">
        {% for status in checkInStatuses %}
            <div class="rstat {{ status.isActive ? '' : 'off' }}">
                <span class="ord">{{ status.isActive ? loop.index : '—' }}</span>
                <span class="nm"><b>{{ status.label }}</b><span class="key">{{ status.key }}</span></span>
                <span class="kind">{{ status.kind.label }}</span>
                <span class="st">
                    {%- if status.isActive %}
                        offered on the handset
                        {%- if status.kind.value == 'at_post' %} · verified / unverified derive from this one{% endif %}
                    {%- else %}
                        retired &mdash; kept, because a past day has to keep the word that described it
                    {%- endif %}
                </span>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="rfrag"><b>This area offers no check-in status</b><em>a ranger with nothing to declare cannot check in, so presence cannot be derived at all &mdash; the area&rsquo;s own configure page is where the list is written</em></div>
        {% endfor %}
        <div class="rfrag"><b>Not this module&rsquo;s to write</b><em>a check-in belongs to the area, and so do the statuses it can carry &mdash; the roster reads them and derives presence from them</em></div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
